class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Trsm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.trsmRight\">trsmRight</a> <span class=\"fn\">uplo</span> <span class=\"fn\">d</span> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">A</span> <span class=\"fn\">B</span>)</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.data\">data</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a>   <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.mapMat\">mapMat</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">B</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.data\">data</a></span> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">B</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.off\">off</a></span> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">B</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.ld\">ld</a></span> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">0</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">fun (<span class=\"fn\">i</span> <span class=\"fn\">j</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>) (<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>) =&gt; <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Trsm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.trsmRightAt\">trsmRightAt</a> <span class=\"fn\">uplo</span> <span class=\"fn\">d</span> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">A</span> <span class=\"fn\">B</span> <span class=\"fn\">i</span> <span class=\"fn\">j</span></span></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The array of `trsmRight uplo d α A B` is the array of `B` with its elements solved.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float32/Trsm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.data_trsmRight","kind":"theorem","line":1495,"name":"BLAS.Float32.Mat.data_trsmRight","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float32/Trsm.lean#L1495-L1499"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Trsm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.trsmRight\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">trsmRight</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">uplo</span> : <a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Trsv.html#BLAS.Float32.Uplo\">Uplo</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">d</span> : <a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Trsv.html#BLAS.Float32.Diag\">Diag</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">A</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">B</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`trsmRight uplo d α A B` solves `X * A = α * B` for the triangle `uplo` of `A`, with a unit\ndiagonal if `d` is `.unit`, over `B`, by the loops of the reference BLAS: for the upper triangle,\nfor each column `j` of `B` from `0` to `n - 1`, it scales the column by `α`, subtracts `A[k, j]`\ntimes column `k` for `k = 0, …, j - 1`, and divides it by `A[j, j]` unless the diagonal is unit;\nfor the lower triangle, it does the same from `j = n - 1` down to `0`, with `k = j + 1, …, n - 1`.\nIt updates `B` in place when its array is not shared, and leaves the elements of the array outside\n`B` unchanged. As in the reference BLAS, it sets `B` to `0` without reading `A` or `B` when\n`α = 0`, reads only the triangle `uplo` of `A`, and doesn't check for a zero on the diagonal.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float32/Trsm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.trsmRight","kind":"def","line":1477,"name":"BLAS.Float32.Mat.trsmRight","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float32/Trsm.lean#L1477-L1493"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Trsm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.trsmRightData_eq\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">trsmRightData_eq</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">uplo</span> : <a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Trsv.html#BLAS.Float32.Uplo\">Uplo</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">d</span> : <a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Trsv.html#BLAS.Float32.Diag\">Diag</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">A</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">B</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <s