ray/Float32/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Float32Array\">ScalarArray.Float32Array</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hb</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">b</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Float32/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Float32Array.size\">size</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">sz</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./ScalarArray/Float32/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Float32Array\">ScalarArray.Float32Array</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The loop of `trsm` over the columns from `j`, on the array `b` of an `m × n` matrix: it scales\ncolumn `j` by `α`, then solves it by `trsv`, or solves the columns `j` to `j + 3` together by\n`trsm4Data` when they are in `B`. It takes the offset and the leading dimension of the\nmatrix rather than the matrix, which would keep a second reference to its array.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float32/Trsm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.trsmLoop","kind":"def","line":797,"name":"BLAS.Float32.Mat.trsmLoop","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float32/Trsm.lean#L797-L817"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Trsm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.colOf\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">colOf</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">off </span><span class=\"fn\">ld </span><span class=\"fn\">sz</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hsz</span> : <sp